    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-10T04:10:35+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-10T04:10:35+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-09T17:40:35Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-09T17:40:35Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system briefly establishes in the north today. Another series of troughs and cold fronts are expected to enter western SA early on Sunday, crossing the state and then clearing in the east by the end of Monday. A ridge of high pressure will then push into western SA on Monday before the associated high moves into waters south on Tuesday. A trough over the WA/NT border will also extend into SA at times from Monday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW008" description="Mid North" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-10T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-11T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-09T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-10T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower this morning. Winds westerly 20 to 30 km/h becoming light in the evening. Daytime maximum temperatures between 19 and 23.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">No Rating</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:40am to 4:30pm, UV Index predicted to reach 8 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-11T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-12T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-10T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-11T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny morning. High chance of showers in the afternoon and evening. The chance of a thunderstorm in the afternoon and evening. Winds north to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h turning northwesterly 25 to 35 km/h in the middle of the day then decreasing to 15 to 25 km/h in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to around 8 with daytime temperatures reaching around 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-12T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-13T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-11T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-12T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Medium chance of showers, most likely in the morning. The chance of a thunderstorm in the morning. Winds west to northwesterly 15 to 20 km/h turning south to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 10 and 13 with daytime temperatures reaching between 17 and 21.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-13T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-14T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-12T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-13T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Winds southerly 15 to 25 km/h turning southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 4 and 7 with daytime temperatures reaching between 16 and 20.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
